1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,886
Every morning at the Corner Cafe, Asha
writes her jobs on a scrap of paper.

2
00:00:05,906 --> 00:00:06,942
Open the cafe.

3
00:00:06,962 --> 00:00:07,922
Restock milk.

4
00:00:07,942 --> 00:00:09,280
Call the supplier.

5
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,371
By lunch, the paper is lost, and nobody
knows what is done.

6
00:00:13,987 --> 00:00:15,667
Welcome to Chapter 28.

7
00:00:15,687 --> 00:00:16,826
The final boss!

8
00:00:16,846 --> 00:00:19,841
In Chapter 1, Asha printed one receipt.

9
00:00:19,861 --> 00:00:22,237
Today she builds real software.

10
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:27,512
Asha will build a task manager that keeps
her jobs in a file, with tests written

11
00:00:27,532 --> 00:00:30,277
first, and an AI assistant at every stage.

12
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,316
The AI will promise that its code passes
all of her tests.

13
00:00:34,336 --> 00:00:35,847
Her tests will decide.

14
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:37,853
Here is the mission.

15
00:00:37,873 --> 00:00:40,700
Add a task, with a title and a priority.

16
00:00:40,733 --> 00:00:42,953
Done marks a task as finished.

17
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,254
List shows every task, and quit saves them
in a file, so they are still there

18
00:00:48,274 --> 00:00:48,870
tomorrow.

19
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:52,704
And a broken file gives a clear message,
never a crash.

20
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:56,670
This is the final boss, so it uses the
whole course.

21
00:00:56,690 --> 00:00:59,910
Printing, text and input, from the first
chapters.

22
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:01,523
Decisions and loops.

23
00:01:01,567 --> 00:01:04,117
Lists, dictionaries and comprehensions.

24
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:07,397
Functions, modules, and tests written
first.

25
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:10,173
Files, error handling and JSON.

26
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:15,268
And classes, from Chapter 26, with the
safe changes from Chapter 27.

27
00:01:15,850 --> 00:01:21,310
Tasks core holds the rules: a task, a task
list, and saving and loading.

28
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:23,652
The test file checks the rules.

29
00:01:23,672 --> 00:01:24,783
It comes first.

30
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:27,903
Task app holds the conversation with the
user.

31
00:01:27,933 --> 00:01:31,596
And tasks dot JSON keeps the tasks between
runs.

32
00:01:32,187 --> 00:01:33,842
Here is a real session.

33
00:01:33,862 --> 00:01:35,372
Asha lists her tasks.

34
00:01:35,392 --> 00:01:40,837
Each line shows a number, an x for a done
task, the title and the priority.

35
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:44,397
She marks task 2 as done, and adds a new
task.

36
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:46,780
The second list shows both changes.

37
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,673
Quit saves them in the file.

38
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:52,090
Asha writes down what done means.

39
00:01:52,133 --> 00:01:52,437
One.

40
00:01:52,457 --> 00:01:57,613
Add refuses an empty title, or a priority
that is not 1, 2 or 3.

41
00:01:57,633 --> 00:01:58,365
Two and three.

42
00:01:58,385 --> 00:02:00,352
Done takes a number, counting from 1.

43
00:02:00,372 --> 00:02:01,547
List shows every task.

44
00:02:01,567 --> 00:02:02,587
Four and five.

45
00:02:02,607 --> 00:02:04,221
Quit saves every task.

46
00:02:04,241 --> 00:02:07,416
A missing or empty file means no tasks
yet.

47
00:02:07,436 --> 00:02:10,017
A broken file gives one clear line.

48
00:02:10,067 --> 00:02:10,372
Six.

49
00:02:10,392 --> 00:02:13,627
The rules contain no input and no print.

50
00:02:13,667 --> 00:02:14,516
And seven.

51
00:02:14,536 --> 00:02:16,167
All ten tests pass.

52
00:02:16,787 --> 00:02:18,775
Quick check, from Chapter 20.

53
00:02:18,795 --> 00:02:21,268
Why must the rules contain no input?

54
00:02:32,647 --> 00:02:32,768
B.

55
00:02:32,788 --> 00:02:34,106
A test cannot type.

56
00:02:34,126 --> 00:02:37,699
A rule that waits for a person would stop
the test.

57
00:02:37,719 --> 00:02:40,658
So the conversation lives in its own file.

58
00:02:41,253 --> 00:02:42,185
Take a breather.

59
00:02:42,205 --> 00:02:44,563
You know the files, and what done means.

60
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,885
Next, Asha plans with an AI assistant.

61
00:02:52,617 --> 00:02:56,959
In this project, the six AI stages help
build one module: the rules.

62
00:02:56,979 --> 00:02:57,857
Stage 1: plan.

63
00:02:57,877 --> 00:03:00,937
Asha says what she wants, and says: no
code yet.

64
00:03:00,967 --> 00:03:06,988
The AI suggests one class whose run method
asks with input, prints the tasks, and

65
00:03:07,008 --> 00:03:08,107
saves the file.

66
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:09,023
It would work.

67
00:03:09,043 --> 00:03:13,898
But nothing in it could be tested, because
every method waits for a person.

68
00:03:13,918 --> 00:03:16,043
Asha remembers her criterion six.

69
00:03:16,067 --> 00:03:20,576
So she asks for the rules in one module,
with no input and no print, and the

70
00:03:20,596 --> 00:03:22,484
conversation in a separate file.

71
00:03:23,083 --> 00:03:24,078
Time to build.

72
00:03:24,098 --> 00:03:29,224
Step 1: as in Chapter 20, Asha writes ten
tests before any rule exists.

73
00:03:29,244 --> 00:03:33,283
Sample makes a list of three tasks for the
tests to use.

74
00:03:33,333 --> 00:03:36,973
The first test checks that tasks keep
their order.

75
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,142
The second checks that an empty title is
refused, with pytest raises, from Chapter

76
00:03:43,162 --> 00:03:43,367
22.

77
00:03:43,987 --> 00:03:45,837
Then she writes empty rules.

78
00:03:45,857 --> 00:03:49,377
The classes and functions exist, but they
do nothing.

79
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:54,925
Open tasks and lines give back an empty
list, and load tasks gives back an empty

80
00:03:54,945 --> 00:03:55,618
task list.

81
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:07,200
No.

82
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:08,962
Asha runs them to see.

83
00:04:09,553 --> 00:04:11,548
Seven fail, as they should.

84
00:04:11,568 --> 00:04:13,263
But three pass already.

85
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:15,638
An empty list looks like no tasks.

86
00:04:15,658 --> 00:04:21,185
So the tests for a missing file and an
empty file pass on rules that do nothing.

87
00:04:21,205 --> 00:04:22,710
So does the save test.

88
00:04:22,733 --> 00:04:26,108
A passing test proves something only when
it can fail.

89
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:27,241
Step 2.

90
00:04:27,261 --> 00:04:34,093
A task is a data class, as in Chapter 26:
a title, a priority that starts at 2, and

91
00:04:34,113 --> 00:04:36,404
done, which starts as False.

92
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:39,849
The task list keeps the tasks in a list.

93
00:04:39,869 --> 00:04:45,121
Tasks or empty list gives the list that
was passed in, or a new empty one.

94
00:04:45,141 --> 00:04:47,970
List makes a copy, so nothing is shared.

95
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,110
Add strips the spaces around the title
first.

96
00:04:51,133 --> 00:04:56,916
Then it refuses an empty title, and a
priority that is not 1, 2 or 3, each with

97
00:04:56,936 --> 00:04:58,385
its own value error.

98
00:04:58,987 --> 00:05:00,796
Asha adds three tasks.

99
00:05:00,816 --> 00:05:06,117
Line 6 adds Restock milk with spaces
around it, and no priority.

100
00:05:06,167 --> 00:05:11,927
Line 9 prints one line per task: its
number, a box that is empty until the task

101
00:05:11,947 --> 00:05:15,146
is done, the title, and P with the
priority.

102
00:05:26,513 --> 00:05:31,593
2, the title without spaces, and P2, the
default priority.

103
00:05:31,633 --> 00:05:36,390
And the empty title on line 11 is refused,
with the message from add.

104
00:05:36,983 --> 00:05:37,474
Step 3.

105
00:05:37,494 --> 00:05:42,576
People count tasks from 1, but a list
counts from 0, as in Chapter 11.

106
00:05:42,596 --> 00:05:47,823
Complete checks the number first, then
marks the task at number minus 1.

107
00:05:47,867 --> 00:05:52,607
Open tasks keeps the tasks that are not
done, with a comprehension.

108
00:05:52,633 --> 00:05:58,434
Lines makes one line per task: its number,
an x when it is done, the title and the

109
00:05:58,454 --> 00:05:59,073
priority.

110
00:05:59,687 --> 00:06:01,583
Asha completes task 1.

111
00:06:01,602 --> 00:06:03,847
The first task gets its x.

112
00:06:03,867 --> 00:06:05,750
Two open tasks are left.

113
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:09,241
And task 4 does not exist, so it is
refused.

114
00:06:09,853 --> 00:06:10,881
Stage 2: write.

115
00:06:10,901 --> 00:06:13,257
Asha wrote complete herself first.

116
00:06:13,277 --> 00:06:18,987
Now she asks the AI for the same rule, as
a small function she can test alone, and

117
00:06:19,007 --> 00:06:20,803
says: people count from 1.

118
00:06:20,833 --> 00:06:24,615
The AI's version is one line, and it
sounds sure.

119
00:06:24,635 --> 00:06:29,269
Asha names it ai complete, so both
versions fit in one file.

120
00:06:29,887 --> 00:06:32,329
She puts both versions in one file.

121
00:06:32,349 --> 00:06:35,777
Each one completes task 1 on a list of two
tasks.

122
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:38,844
Look at line 12 of the AI's version.

123
00:06:50,213 --> 00:06:52,508
Restock milk, the second task.

124
00:06:52,528 --> 00:06:55,593
Position 1 in a list is the second item.

125
00:06:55,633 --> 00:06:59,644
Asha's version subtracts 1, so it marks
the first task.

126
00:06:59,664 --> 00:07:00,963
She keeps her own.

127
00:07:01,553 --> 00:07:02,194
Breather.

128
00:07:02,214 --> 00:07:03,735
Relax your shoulders.

129
00:07:03,755 --> 00:07:05,203
The task list works.

130
00:07:05,233 --> 00:07:09,704
Next, saving and loading, written by the
AI against her tests.

131
00:07:14,450 --> 00:07:16,209
Step 4: save and load.

132
00:07:16,229 --> 00:07:17,664
Stage 3: generate.

133
00:07:17,684 --> 00:07:22,920
Asha pastes her ten tests, and asks the AI
for the two functions.

134
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:24,780
Do not change my tests.

135
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:29,146
The AI writes both, and says: they pass
all ten of your tests.

136
00:07:29,753 --> 00:07:34,473
Line 47 gives the list of tasks straight
to JSON dumps.

137
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:40,318
And load tasks reads the text and gives it
to JSON loads, with no other check.

138
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:51,894
No.

139
00:07:51,914 --> 00:07:53,457
Asha does not argue.

140
00:07:53,477 --> 00:07:54,942
She runs her tests.

141
00:07:55,553 --> 00:07:56,266
Two fail.

142
00:07:56,286 --> 00:07:59,113
Save then load, and the empty file.

143
00:07:59,133 --> 00:08:02,027
Eight pass, but a promise of ten is not
ten.

144
00:08:02,047 --> 00:08:04,344
Her tests caught a confident claim.

145
00:08:04,917 --> 00:08:06,554
Step 5: the command loop.

146
00:08:06,574 --> 00:08:08,675
Task app holds the conversation.

147
00:08:08,695 --> 00:08:13,845
Run asks for a command until the user
types quit, then returns, which ends the

148
00:08:13,865 --> 00:08:14,177
loop.

149
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:17,730
Add asks for a title and a priority, and
calls the rule.

150
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:19,318
Done asks for a number.

151
00:08:19,338 --> 00:08:20,822
List prints each line.

152
00:08:20,842 --> 00:08:23,077
Anything else shows the commands.

153
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:27,118
Every rule raises only value error, with a
clear message.

154
00:08:27,138 --> 00:08:31,864
So one except catches a bad title, a bad
priority and a bad number.

155
00:08:32,487 --> 00:08:34,849
The main program loads the tasks.

156
00:08:34,869 --> 00:08:39,397
A broken file gives one line that starts
with tasks not loaded.

157
00:08:39,433 --> 00:08:42,703
The else block runs only when the tasks
loaded.

158
00:08:42,723 --> 00:08:46,412
It shows how many are open, runs the loop,
and saves.

159
00:08:46,983 --> 00:08:47,940
Stage 4: test.

160
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:53,383
Asha asks the AI for test cases for
loading, with an expected result for each.

161
00:08:53,433 --> 00:08:57,394
It lists a normal file, a missing file and
a broken file.

162
00:08:57,414 --> 00:09:02,353
And it says: an empty file is broken JSON,
so it should raise an error.

163
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:07,373
Asha's criterion five says the opposite:
an empty file means no tasks yet.

164
00:09:07,393 --> 00:09:11,760
Her test already checks it, and it is one
of the two that failed.

165
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:15,606
Where the AI and her criteria disagree,
her criteria win.

166
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,391
Stage 5: debug.

167
00:09:17,411 --> 00:09:22,313
For the other failure, Asha saves one task
with the AI's code.

168
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:28,030
It stops with a long error report, through
the lines of the JSON module.

169
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:32,904
As she learned in Chapter 1, she finds the
error line at the bottom.

170
00:09:32,924 --> 00:09:36,975
Type error: object of type Task is not
JSON serializable.

171
00:09:36,995 --> 00:09:40,047
Serializable means it can be saved as
text.

172
00:09:40,067 --> 00:09:42,623
Here you see only that error line.

173
00:09:42,643 --> 00:09:48,686
On your computer, the report above it
shows full file paths, and Python 3.14 and

174
00:09:48,706 --> 00:09:51,112
newer add a short note under it.

175
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:57,200
She pastes the code and the error, and
asks for the cause first.

176
00:09:57,233 --> 00:10:02,206
The AI explains: JSON can save numbers,
text, true and false, None, lists and

177
00:10:02,226 --> 00:10:03,049
dictionaries.

178
00:10:03,069 --> 00:10:04,605
A task is none of these.

179
00:10:04,625 --> 00:10:09,014
So each task becomes a dictionary first,
with a new method, to dict.

180
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:14,320
The new to dict method returns a task as a
dictionary.

181
00:10:14,367 --> 00:10:19,307
Line 53 turns each task into a dictionary
before dumps.

182
00:10:19,333 --> 00:10:25,673
And lines 64 and 65 treat an empty file as
no tasks, before JSON loads can complain.

183
00:10:26,287 --> 00:10:30,451
Then she runs every test again, not only
the two that failed.

184
00:10:30,471 --> 00:10:31,206
Ten passed.

185
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:33,685
One more check, by hand.

186
00:10:33,705 --> 00:10:36,905
Asha saves two tasks, the first one done.

187
00:10:36,925 --> 00:10:41,461
Line 10 prints the saved file, and line 11
loads it again.

188
00:10:52,813 --> 00:10:58,613
The same two lines as before saving: task
1 with its x, and task 2 still open.

189
00:10:58,633 --> 00:11:01,986
And the file shows each task as a
dictionary.

190
00:11:02,006 --> 00:11:05,208
JSON writes True as true, in small
letters.

191
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:06,640
Quick check.

192
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:09,789
Which of these can JSON dumps save, as it
is?

193
00:11:21,147 --> 00:11:21,268
C.

194
00:11:21,288 --> 00:11:24,026
A dictionary of text, numbers and true.

195
00:11:24,046 --> 00:11:27,420
Any other object must become a dictionary
first.

196
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:31,447
Last, Asha runs the whole program on three
cases.

197
00:11:31,467 --> 00:11:34,050
She writes the expected result first.

198
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:36,750
A first run, with no file yet.

199
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,070
Bad answers.

200
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:39,566
And a broken file.

201
00:11:40,187 --> 00:11:42,728
No file yet, so zero open tasks.

202
00:11:42,748 --> 00:11:45,449
She adds one, lists it, and quits.

203
00:11:45,469 --> 00:11:45,850
Pass.

204
00:11:46,453 --> 00:11:47,681
Now bad answers.

205
00:11:47,701 --> 00:11:49,708
First, a priority of high.

206
00:11:49,728 --> 00:11:55,244
Line 18 turns the answer into a whole
number with int, as in Chapter 4.

207
00:12:06,613 --> 00:12:12,127
Int raises a value error, and line 28
prints not done, with Python's own

208
00:12:12,147 --> 00:12:12,742
message.

209
00:12:12,762 --> 00:12:13,433
No crash.

210
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:16,618
An empty title and task 9 are refused too.

211
00:12:16,638 --> 00:12:20,394
And an unknown command shows the list of
commands.

212
00:12:20,414 --> 00:12:20,772
Pass.

213
00:12:21,387 --> 00:12:25,906
And the broken file, which is missing a
comma between two tasks.

214
00:12:25,926 --> 00:12:29,452
Load tasks raises a value error for a
broken file.

215
00:12:40,813 --> 00:12:41,052
No.

216
00:12:41,072 --> 00:12:45,276
Line 34 prints one clear line: expecting a
comma.

217
00:12:45,296 --> 00:12:45,707
Pass.

218
00:12:45,727 --> 00:12:47,086
All three match.

219
00:12:47,687 --> 00:12:48,271
Breather.

220
00:12:48,291 --> 00:12:51,497
Every test passes, and every known case
matches.

221
00:12:51,533 --> 00:12:55,150
Next, the last stage: a review from the
AI.

222
00:12:59,883 --> 00:13:01,128
Stage 6: improve.

223
00:13:01,148 --> 00:13:02,541
All ten tests pass.

224
00:13:02,561 --> 00:13:08,416
Asha asks for one change that makes the
module shorter, and says: do not change

225
00:13:08,436 --> 00:13:09,383
what it does.

226
00:13:09,433 --> 00:13:13,160
The AI says: remove the priority check
from add.

227
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:15,658
The app already asks for 1 to 3.

228
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:18,007
Remember her third test.

229
00:13:18,027 --> 00:13:22,292
It adds a task with priority 5, and
expects a value error.

230
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:33,892
No.

231
00:13:33,912 --> 00:13:37,337
One fails: the test for a bad priority.

232
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:40,206
The app's question only asks for 1 to 3.

233
00:13:40,226 --> 00:13:45,925
It cannot stop a person who types 5, or
another program that uses the task list.

234
00:13:45,945 --> 00:13:48,927
The suggestion changed what the code does.

235
00:13:48,947 --> 00:13:50,572
Asha keeps her version.

236
00:13:51,187 --> 00:13:54,137
Here are all six stages, on one module of
rules.

237
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:58,207
The AI helped at every stage, from the
plan to the improvement.

238
00:13:58,233 --> 00:14:00,315
It was confidently wrong five times.

239
00:14:00,335 --> 00:14:02,183
A plan that could not be tested.

240
00:14:02,233 --> 00:14:03,443
The wrong task.

241
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:06,587
A promise of ten passes.

242
00:14:06,633 --> 00:14:08,973
A case list with no empty file.

243
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,070
And a check it wanted to remove.

244
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,590
At debug, the AI was right.

245
00:14:12,610 --> 00:14:15,610
Asha could tell, because the fix made
every test pass.

246
00:14:15,633 --> 00:14:20,598
Every time, something Asha wrote first
decided: her criteria, a side by side run,

247
00:14:20,618 --> 00:14:21,459
and her tests.

248
00:14:22,053 --> 00:14:23,060
Last breather.

249
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:28,853
Before she pasted any code into the chat,
Asha checked it for private data, the

250
00:14:28,873 --> 00:14:30,393
habit from Chapter 1.

251
00:14:30,413 --> 00:14:32,593
Her tasks hold only cafe jobs.

252
00:14:32,633 --> 00:14:33,698
Let's recap.

253
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:40,950
Here is what you used in the final boss.

254
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:46,910
Keep the rules free of input and print, so
tests can check them.

255
00:14:46,933 --> 00:14:48,280
Write the tests first.

256
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:51,323
A test that passes on empty rules proves
nothing.

257
00:14:51,367 --> 00:14:56,467
Number tasks from 1 for people, and
subtract 1 for the list.

258
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,859
JSON saves dictionaries, not objects.

259
00:14:58,879 --> 00:15:00,980
To dict turns one into the other.

260
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,765
A missing or empty file can mean nothing
yet.

261
00:15:03,785 --> 00:15:05,870
A broken one gets a clear message.

262
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:11,821
And every AI suggestion was judged by your
criteria, a run, or your tests.

263
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:13,533
One last check.

264
00:15:13,553 --> 00:15:17,006
An AI says its new code passes all your
tests.

265
00:15:17,026 --> 00:15:18,139
What do you do?

266
00:15:29,513 --> 00:15:29,644
A.

267
00:15:29,664 --> 00:15:31,372
Run the tests yourself.

268
00:15:31,392 --> 00:15:33,325
A promise is not a result.

269
00:15:33,345 --> 00:15:34,677
Your tests decide.

270
00:15:35,287 --> 00:15:36,831
Final boss complete!

271
00:15:36,851 --> 00:15:40,508
You earned 300 XP and the Python Builder
badge.

272
00:15:40,528 --> 00:15:43,560
Module 6 is done, and so is the course.

273
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:47,270
Look how far you came.

274
00:15:47,290 --> 00:15:50,543
In Chapter 1, Asha printed one cafe
receipt.

275
00:15:50,567 --> 00:15:54,297
Then variables, text and input, and the
Bill Splitter.

276
00:15:54,333 --> 00:15:59,083
Decisions, loops and debugging, and the
Guessing Game.

277
00:15:59,133 --> 00:16:03,533
Lists, dictionaries, tuples and sets, and
the Expense Tracker.

278
00:16:03,567 --> 00:16:05,880
Functions, modules and tests, and the Quiz
App.

279
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:10,770
Files, errors, JSON and packages, and the
Report Generator.

280
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:15,200
And classes, safe changes, and today's
task manager.

281
00:16:15,233 --> 00:16:19,401
28 chapters, 6 boss levels, and one AI
habit: check every answer.

282
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:24,580
The practice file has eight more tasks,
worth 170 XP.

283
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:29,600
Three warm-ups, worth 10 XP each, such as
JSON there and back.

284
00:16:29,633 --> 00:16:34,233
Three apply tasks, worth 20 each,
including removing a task.

285
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:39,078
And two stretch tasks, worth 40 each,
including a load that never crashes.

286
00:16:39,650 --> 00:16:40,623
So, what's next?

287
00:16:40,643 --> 00:16:41,492
Keep building.

288
00:16:41,512 --> 00:16:46,643
Pick a small problem from your own life,
plan it, write the tests first, and let an

289
00:16:46,663 --> 00:16:47,140
AI help.

290
00:16:47,167 --> 00:16:50,371
When a topic feels unclear, go back to its
chapter.

291
00:16:50,391 --> 00:16:52,837
And try the practice tasks you skipped.

292
00:16:52,867 --> 00:16:54,535
Do the warm-up tasks now.

293
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,427
They take about ten minutes.

294
00:16:56,467 --> 00:16:59,745
Thank you for learning with Asha at the
Corner Cafe.

295
00:16:59,765 --> 00:17:00,570
Happy coding!
